# 0002. Use Generated API Contracts

Status: {% if include_api_contract | default(false) %}Accepted{% else %}Deferred{% endif %}

## Context

Frontend/backend API drift is easy to miss when DTOs are copied by hand. A single DTO/source-of-truth strategy gives agents and humans a concrete artifact to compare.

## Decision

{% if include_api_contract | default(false) -%}
Generate backend OpenAPI and frontend API TypeScript types with `./scripts/generate-api-contract.sh`.

`./scripts/validate-changed-scope.mjs` runs contract checks when API/schema files are affected. `./scripts/finalize.sh` runs `./scripts/check-api-contract.sh` as part of the full gate to confirm committed generated artifacts are current.
{% else -%}
Generated API contracts are not enabled yet for this project shape. If a backend/frontend API boundary becomes important, choose one DTO/source-of-truth strategy and add generation plus freshness scripts before relying on frontend API shapes.
{% endif %}
## Consequences

{% if include_api_contract | default(false) -%}
- Backend API changes must include generated contract diffs.
- Frontend code should import generated API types instead of hand-writing backend response shapes.
- Contract freshness failures should explain how to regenerate the artifacts.
{% else -%}
- The project should not treat any generated schema as authoritative until a generation script and freshness check exist.
- This decision should be updated when generated contracts are enabled.
{% endif -%}
